1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,060
We've all done it. We buy something we think we like and then change our minds about it.
我们都做过这样的事：买下自认为喜欢的东西，之后又改变主意。

2
00:00:06,060 --> 00:00:14,480
Whether panic buying, an impulse purchase or shopper's remorse, we're fortunate many companies allow us to easily exchange or refund items.
无论是恐慌性购买、冲动消费还是购物后悔，幸运的是许多公司允许我们轻松退换或退款。

3
00:00:14,480 --> 00:00:23,560
In fact it's so easy these days that retailers are seeing an increase in a new type of shopper: the serial returner.
事实上，如今退货如此便捷，零售商发现一种新型购物者在增多：习惯性退货者。

4
00:00:23,560 --> 00:00:31,210
A serial returner is someone who buys items, often in bulk, only to return most of them.
习惯性退货者是指购买物品（常为批量购买）后却退回大部分的人。

5
00:00:31,210 --> 00:00:45,830
41-year-old Hester Grainger, founder of Mumala Club, estimates spending £300 to £400 each month on clothes, but returning "around 80%", she told the BBC.
41岁的赫斯特・格兰杰是Mumala Club创始人，她告诉BBC，自己每月估计花300到400英镑买衣服，但会退回“约80%”。

6
00:00:45,830 --> 00:00:48,230
This isn't unique.
这并非个例。

7
00:00:48,230 --> 00:01:06,560
Barclaycard, which processes nearly half of the UK's credit and debit card transactions, says that in the last two years 26% of retailers have seen an increase in in-store and online returns – with the number of items being sent back up by 22%.
处理英国近一半信用卡和借记卡交易的巴克莱卡公司表示，过去两年里，26%的零售商发现线下和线上退货量增加——退回物品数量上升了22%。

8
00:01:06,560 --> 00:01:09,240
It's a problem for companies.
这对企业是个问题。

9
00:01:09,240 --> 00:01:11,940
Handling these returns eats into profits.
处理这些退货会侵蚀利润。

10
00:01:11,940 --> 00:01:16,440
Free delivery for the customer means the company foots the bill.
顾客享受免费配送意味着公司买单。

11
00:01:16,440 --> 00:01:22,730
Items may need to be repackaged. They are damaged - making them unfit for resale.
物品可能需要重新包装，若已损坏则无法再售。

12
00:01:22,730 --> 00:01:36,840
Tony Mannix, CEO of Clipper, a logistics firm that handles returned goods for major retailers, said about 5% of them end up "being binned." Sometimes the fast fashion cycle has moved on.
为大型零售商处理退货的物流公司Clipper的首席执行官托尼・曼尼克斯称，约5%的退货最终“被扔进垃圾桶”。

13
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:45,660
By the time the item comes back, it becomes a cut-price item on a reduced-to-clear rail - at further loss to the company.
有时快时尚周期已更新，当物品退回时，只能作为清仓打折商品——公司进一步亏损。

14
00:01:45,660 --> 00:01:49,830
Some companies are taking action to deter this behaviour.
一些公司正采取行动遏制这种行为。

15
00:01:49,830 --> 00:01:59,230
According to a BBC article, four in ten retailers now say they charge for returns to discourage the sending of non-faulty items.
BBC一篇文章称，十分之四的零售商表示现在对退货收费，以阻止非瑕疵商品的退回。

16
00:01:59,230 --> 00:02:06,790
Online retail giant Amazon was reported to have started barring customers with too many returned items.
据报道，在线零售巨头亚马逊已开始禁止顾客过多地退货。

17
00:02:06,790 --> 00:02:15,740
This is something a study by retail management system Brightpearl found over half of UK fashion retailers would consider.
零售管理系统Brightpearl的研究发现，超半数英国时尚零售商会考虑这一做法。

18
00:02:15,740 --> 00:02:21,640
And Barclaycard says a third of retailers have hiked their prices to cover these returns.
巴克莱卡公司称，三分之一的零售商已涨价以弥补退货成本。

19
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:31,710
But Vicky Brock, director of data innovation at ReBound Returns, a returns management software system, believes this isn't the best strategy.
但退货管理软件系统ReBound Returns的数据创新总监维姬・布洛克认为，这并非最佳策略。

20
00:02:31,710 --> 00:02:38,840
Speaking in a BBC article, she says discouraging returns shows a lack of understanding by the retailer.
她在BBC文章中表示，阻止退货表明零售商缺乏同理心。

21
00:02:38,840 --> 00:02:44,400
Using data, companies can reduce returns by helping customers choose better.
利用数据，公司可通过帮助顾客更好地选择来减少退货。

22
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:55,370
Some companies such as Uniqlo and Asos already provide a suggested size based on the customer's previous purchases and information on height and weight.
优衣库和Asos等公司已根据顾客过往购买记录及身高体重信息提供尺码建议。

23
00:02:55,370 --> 00:03:06,000
Ultimately, she says, returns are now as much a part of the shopping experience as buying things, and shops need to take this into consideration.
她称，从根本上说，退货如今和购物一样是消费体验的一部分，商家需要考虑这一点。
